<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka rupee closes soft on speculation.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka rupee closes soft on speculation.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Speculative buying of dollars kept the Sri Lanka rupee down in thin trade on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The rupee closed at 57.65 to the dollar after opening at 57.62, they said.</p>
<p>&quot;Speculators were the most active in the market where there was hardly any commercial demand,&quot; said a Deutsche Bank dealer.</p>
<p>Overnight call money rates closed at 10 percent after opening at 10.5 percent, he said.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941 434319)</p>
